@quality-metrics
Scenario: Result Quality Validation
  Given a set of test queries with known ground truth
  When evaluating search results:
    ```javascript
    const metrics = {
      contextRelevance: async (result, query) => {
        const score = await evaluateRelevance(result.context, query)
        expect(score).toBeGreaterThan(0.8)
      },
      resultFaithfulness: async (result, groundTruth) => {
        const faithfulness = await comparePaths(result.path, groundTruth.path)
        expect(faithfulness).toBeGreaterThan(0.9)
      }
    }
    ```
  Then measure quality metrics:
    | Metric            | Target | Measurement Method                     |
    | NDCG@10          | > 0.8  | Normalized Discounted Cumulative Gain |
    | MRR              | > 0.7  | Mean Reciprocal Rank                  |
    | Path Precision   | > 0.9  | Correct relationships / total         |

